meta {
  name: 05-Look at my own public profile (the way an owner would see me)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/api/users/{{emeka_user_id}}/profile
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{emeka_jwt}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.role: eq AGENT
}

docs {
  Critical for me — this is what owners see when deciding to hire me.
  I want to see: verified badge? rating? closed-deal count? response
  rate? Per the schema, I get name, role, identityVerifiedAt,
  agentCredentialVerifiedAt, suspended, averageRating, reviewCount,
  joinedAt.

  No closedDealCount. No responseRate. No "active listings" count. No
  bio. No photo. No service area (Port Harcourt). For an agent who
  lives or dies by signals, this is a thin profile.
}
